# Root .dockerignore — applies to any build whose context is the platform
# root (api/Dockerfile and, since V2-09, supervisor/Dockerfile — both depend
# on ../contracts as a local path dep, see each Dockerfile's own header).
# Keeps the "sending build context to daemon" step fast; the final images
# only ever COPY the specific paths they need (see each Dockerfile), so this
# is a speed and hygiene measure, not a security boundary on its own — never
# rely on it to keep secrets out of an image, keep those out of the tree
# entirely.

# secrets — never sent to the daemon, never baked into a layer
.env
.env.*
secrets.env
**/secrets.env
*.pem
*.key

# per-package virtualenvs and caches (rebuilt inside the image)
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# node / web (irrelevant to the api image; web/Dockerfile uses web/ as its
# own build context with its own .dockerignore)
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
web/e2e/
web/tests/

# test suites and dev data — not needed at runtime
**/tests/
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal

# vcs / editor / docs
.git/
.gitignore
docs/

# NOTE: do NOT ignore README.md / **/README.md here — contracts/pyproject.toml
# declares `readme = "README.md"` and hatchling reads that file when
# `uv sync --no-editable` builds the lkap-contracts wheel inside
# api/Dockerfile's builder stage; excluding it breaks that build with
# "Readme file does not exist".
